{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c63b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a077f0-8368-79b0-a394-00901144f8f0"},"sequence":376,"recorded_at":1780531400000747,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"b71aae24-19f3-441e-b3e1-6dada05f93d3","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"b71aae24-19f3-441e-b3e1-6dada05f93d3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"b71aae24-19f3-441e-b3e1-6dada05f93d3"},"call_id":"call_01a077f131937122bad4a8b3b4262f57","text":"Read text file `internal/secconftest/skip_fifo_windows.go`.\n1|//go:build windows\n2|\n3|package secconftest\n4|\n5|import \"errors\"\n6|\n7|// makeFifo is unavailable on Windows: named pipes there are not\n8|// filesystem FIFOs and this instrument does not emulate them. The\n9|// fifo probe reports unavailable (and skips, since Windows is not\n10|// strict) instead of pretending.\n11|func makeFifo(dir, name string) (string, error) {\n12|\treturn fifoBuild(dir, name)\n13|}\n14|\n15|// fifoBuild is the seam the probe-honesty test faults. It always\n16|// fails on Windows, matching makeFifo; the test only asserts the\n17|// probe reports the failure honestly.\n18|var fifoBuild = func(dir, name string) (string, error) {\n19|\treturn \"\", errors.New(\"secconftest: named-pipe fixtures are unavailable on Windows\")\n20|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
