link (`O_NOFOLLOW` on unix; an\\n552:Lstat gate refusing symlinks and irregular reparse points with a\\n594:(`src/os/types_windows.go`): `ModeSymlink` for true symlinks and\\n658:rune-for-rune with corpus coverage, plus a symlink-escape commit\\n659:witness gated on a probed capability. Capability probes (`symlink`,\\n660:`fifo`, `mode-bits`, `nonroot`) each really attempt their\\n661:capability — symlink create+Lstat, `mkfifo`+Lstat, `chmod 000`\\n662:denial, uid check — and each gates a named test (symlink-escape\\n663:commit witness, fifo byte-exchange fixture, mode-bits/nonroot denial\\n665:strict platforms where absence is unexpected (symlink and fifo are\\n672:non-root); the final report line witnesses the counters after the\\n869:symlink rules, and recursive submodule state/depth/count constraints that can\\n935:ancestor is a declared `file`, `symlink` or `hardlink` is rejected, reusing the\\n937:path's ancestor set, so a symlink or file parent cannot carry children into\\n978:UTF-8 bytes, including Blob media type, Manifest symlink target, workspace\\n1317:submodule state, sparse-pair drift, and hardlink/symlink/count violations\\n1416:symlink, or not a directory at all are each refused with the immutable digest\\n1437:which is not a symlink, belongs to the effective user and already carries\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 2256,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 564,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
