{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d707","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a077f0-8368-79b0-a394-00901144f8f0"},"sequence":2526,"recorded_at":1780531400005047,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"b71aae24-19f3-441e-b3e1-6dada05f93d3","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"b71aae24-19f3-441e-b3e1-6dada05f93d3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"b71aae24-19f3-441e-b3e1-6dada05f93d3"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"acd3670a-771a-4302-8983-28e0fef37906"},"task_id":"acd3670a-771a-4302-8983-28e0fef37906","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"acd3670a-771a-4302-8983-28e0fef37906","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-84-1\",\n  \"command\": \"head -n 40 LOGBOOK.md; echo \\\"...\\\"; grep -c \\\"^## \\\" LOGBOOK.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Read logbook head and format\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-06\\n\\n### 2155 — secconftest round-3 rework: crashed commit counts as committed, Require wiring pinned, LOGBOOK corrected\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260830-7a0s2c round-3 (review-verdict-rev2, C1/C1b/C2/C2b blocking + 7 unbounded survivors). Production (test instrument) only in `internal/secconftest`: `crash.go` (commit-apply fault finalizes with parked receipt, `ErrPreparePastFinalize`/`ErrCommitPastFinalize`, rollback forgets, staged-missing naming), `skip.go` (`requireT` interface), `main_test.go` (new, `TestMain` final report), `doc.go` (terminal + wiring bounds). Leaf-1 `internal/secprim` untouched.\\n- C1 RULE: a crashed commit counts as committed — the durable write already happened, so rollback is forbidden (`ErrRollbackPastFinalize`) and bytes survive; recovery is via `CommittedBytes`/operator. Driven by `TestTransactorCrashedCommitIsFinal`. C1b neighbours all named (no ENOENT inheritance): rollback-twice, commit-twice, commit-after-rollback, prepare-after-commit refused; prepare-after-rollback restages. Fifth crash point armed through the Transactor (P7 closed).\\n- C2b: `TestRequireSkipArmRecordsVerdict`/`TestRequireFailArmRecordsVerdict` drive the real `Require` through both arms with a recording fake (M04/M05 killed); `TestMain` prints counters after the parallel tests. Round-2's two untrue sentences superseded in the round-3 outcome doc.\\n- C2: 2035 entry corrected in place (false counts withdrawn, digest kept, correction note added); worktree sweep clean.\\n- SURVIVORS CLOSED: M02 (empty-ID with probe), M08 (symlink strictness pinned exactly), M16 (empty operation ID), M27 (whitespace-quote message pin) — all killed. Battery re-derived from this tree: 38 applied / 0 NOT_APPLIED / 0 COMPILE_FAIL / 0 VET_FAIL, 36 killed (narrowing 26 + arm-deletion 6 + census-only 4), 2 survived with bounds: N-DriveRedactNoDelegate (N16 delegation bound) and S1-ModeBitsFalse (survive-as-SKIP). Token-preserving mutant ran the full suite. Manifest `c6018721…` identical after the battery.\\n- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260830-7a0s2c_secconftest-round3.md` (6/6 AC rows, 38-row mutant table, gates with exit codes) + `TASK-260830-7a0s2c_mutant-battery-round3.log` + full-test log.\\n- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (21 pkgs), secconftest `-race` exit 0, `./... -cover` exit 0 (secconftest 92.6%, secprim 94.4%), `go vet` + `GOOS=windows go vet/build` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 (94 cases, unchanged), 8/8 fuzz `-fuzztime=100x` exit 0 with no corpus written, verbose 246 PASS / 0 SKIP / 0 FAIL, digest `5569f34caab734eb`.\\n- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/landing are orchestrator steps).\\n\\n### 2105 — secconftest round-2 rework: C1–C4 closed, instrument stops reporting untrue things\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260830-7a0s2c round-2 (review-verdict-rev1, C1–C4 blocking). Production (test instrument) only in `internal/secconftest`: `crash.go` (finalize gate + `ErrRollbackPastFinalize`, `RemainingArmed`), `skip.go` (`Report()` over live counters, real `mkfifo` fifo probe), `skip_fifo_unix/windows.go` (new, `makeFifo` + fault seam), `hostile.go` untouched, `fuzz_test.go` (no-op poles), `doc.go` (bounds). Leaf-1 `internal/secprim` untouched (`git diff HEAD -- internal/secprim` empty).\\n- C1: `Rollback` now refuses post-commit with `ErrRollbackPastFinalize` and leaves committed bytes intact; `TestTransactorRefusesRollbackPastFinalize` commits-then-rolls-back (the arm it is named for) plus both old arms. Deleting the gate is killed by it (battery A1).\\n- C2: `Report()` reads the live counters; `TestSkipReportReadsRecordedVerdicts` records synthetic verdicts, asserts the report moves, restores state (gutting `recordVerdict` reddens it, battery A4). The round-1 `skipped=0` citation was a constant — genuine datum is 0 `--- SKIP` / 0 `--- FAIL` lines under `go test -v` on darwin non-root, now cited in README/outcome/doc.go.\\n- C3: fifo probe builds a real FIFO (`syscall.Mkfifo`+Lstat; Windows stub unavailable) with a fault seam (`TestSkipFifoProbeAttemptsItsCapability` kills a success-on-failure weakening, battery N14). All 4 probes gate real tests: symlink→escape witness, fifo→byte-exchange fixture, mode-bits+nonroot→denial test (4/4 wired, was 1/4).\\n- C4: all 8 listed survivors closed — digest report/name distinguishing tests (N1–N3), bidi rune-for-rune pin + corpus coverage (N4–N5), Gate pin+drive for all 18 classes (N6), verdict counter test (A4), commit-requires-prepare with planted staged file (A3). Battery re-derived from this tree: 29 applied / 0 NOT_APPLIED / 0 COMPILE_FAIL / 0 VET_FAIL, 27 killed (15 narrowing + 8 arm-deletion + 4 census-only), 2 survived with bounds: N16 driver-delegation (read-verified + arrival-counted) and S1 mode-bits-false (survives-as-SKIP by construction — the SKIP line is the signal). N10 token-preserving mutant killed by the full behavioral suite; tree sha256-identical after the battery.\\n- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260830-7a0s2c_secconftest-round2.md` (6/6 AC rows corrected, 29-row mutant table with bounds, gates with exit codes) + `TASK-260830-7a0s2c_mutant-battery-round2.log` + full-test log.\\n- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (21 pkgs), secconftest `-race` exit 0, `./... -cover` exit 0 (secconftest 89.3%, secprim 94.4% unchanged), `go vet` + `GOOS=windows go vet/build` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 (94 cases, unchanged), 8/8 fuzz `-fuzztime=100x` exit 0 with no corpus written, digest `5569f34caab734eb` x5 processes.\\n- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/landing are orchestrator steps).\\n\\n### 2035 — secconftest instrument leaf: runners, fake clocks, crash points, fuzz, hostile strings, skips\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260830-7a0s2c (second leaf of STORY-260830-1i3qu7). New package `internal/secconftest` (doc/runner/clock/crash/fuzz/hostile/skip + 6 test files): sorted deterministic Runner with execution digest and zero-call refusal, wall-clock-free Fake with Recording wiring detector, CR-MAT-* Injector over a three-phase Transactor with §13.13 outcomes and idempotency_mismatch, 8 Fuzz targets through one shared Driver with seed arrival proofs, 18-class spec-derived hostile roster plus symlink-escape commit witness, 4 probed capabilities with strict-platform failure. Leaf-1 `internal/secprim` production untouched; `task-board.config.json` gains the 8 required fuzz validation commands (pinned by `TestConfiguredValidationRunsEveryFuzzTargetWithFixedBudget`, which failed until registered).\\n- FINDING: the repo already forces fuzz registration — a new Fuzz target without a config line fails `TestConfiguredValidationRunsEveryFuzzTargetWithFixedBudget` plus its coverage parent. The instrument therefore cannot silently add unfuzzed-in-CI targets.\\n- FINDING (M6): a Fake leaking `time.Now` is caught by two fresh fakes disagreeing (real timestamps in the failure), not just by the sleep test — the stronger kill.\\n- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260830-7a0s2c_secconftest.md` (6/6 AC rows with call sites; digest `5569f34caab734eb` x3). CORRECTION (round-3): the mutant counts and the darwin skip citation first written here (10-row table, 10/10 killed, skipped=0) were disproven in round-1 review and are superseded by the round-2 rework entry above and `TASK-260830-7a0s2c_secconftest-round2.md` (29 applied / 2 survivors with bounds; per-test `--- SKIP` lines as the datum).\\n- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (21 pkgs), `-race` exit 0, `-cover` exit 0 (secconftest 86.9%), `go vet` + `GOOS=windows go vet` + `GOOS=windows go build` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 (94 cases, unchanged). 8/8 fuzz targets pass 5s smoke and `-fuzztime=100x` with no corpus written.\\n- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/landing are orchestrator steps).\\n\\n### 1939 — secprim round-3 rework: C1 handle binding, C2 classify-before-close, C3 spelling bound, N24 restored\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260830-2ciy0s round-3 (review-verdict-rev2, C1–C4 blocking). Production: `internal/secprim/nofollow.go` (`guardRootMatches` fstat dev/ino compare via `os.SameFile`, new `guard root mismatch` site in `Guard.Open`); `open_member_unix.go` (classify-before-close at both sites); spelling bound stated in `errors.go`/`inventory_test.go`/README + `TestRefusalInventorySpellingBoundIsStated`; honest reparse mapping in both windows files + README. Tests: `guard_root_test.go` (foreign-handle refusal + matched control, cross-platform), depth-3/4 full-string vectors in `open_unix_test.go`.\\n- ROOT CAUSE (C1): `openCommitRelative(root, _ string, ...)` discarded `guard.root`; unix walked the handle, Windows the path — one entry, two containment roots. Fixed in shared `Guard.Open` so both answer identically.\\n- ROOT CAUSE (C2): from iteration 2 `previous == current`; closing before `classifyCommitErr` fstat'd a recycled fd, misreporting depth>=2 symlink hops as `open failed`. Revert reproduces the exact reported string.\\n- FINDING (N24): arm-drop spelling KILLS (`target special file` vs `target directory`); the `Size() > 0` spelling SURVIVES (empty dirs report Size > 0) — rev2 withdrew the wrong spelling. FINDING (D14): scripted shape is COMPILE-FAIL (unused import), superseded by killing D14b.\\n...\\n7\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 9314,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 2329,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
